For collision \(\vec{V}_{B / A}\) should be along
\(\begin{aligned}
& \overline{\mathrm{B} \rightarrow \mathrm{A}}\left(\overrightarrow{\mathrm{r}}_{\mathrm{A} / \mathrm{B}}\right) \\
& \text { So, } \frac{\overrightarrow{\mathrm{V}}_2-\overrightarrow{\mathrm{V}}_1}{\left|\mathrm{~V}_2-\mathrm{V}_1\right|}=\frac{\overrightarrow{\mathrm{r}}_1-\overrightarrow{\mathrm{r}}_2}{\left|\mathrm{r}_1-\mathrm{r}_2\right|}
\end{aligned}\)
